━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ LiveActions is facet of Checker
    sees Assignments
    sees Comprehensions
    sees Loops
    sees Markup
    sees Styles

_ subscribed-event NamedEvent? = null
_ subscribed-by InstanceId = no-instance

────────────────────
+ do demand
    - callee InstanceId

` Readies what a call reads of a callee. A header that gives the return type is enough, and
` the body stays in the queue. Otherwise the body is typed now, as it is for a statement that a
` finally block watches. A call of a rule under a helper, which may run the rule typed for the
` helper in its place, queues a rule that states its type too, as `promise` says. A callee that
` may not use the heap is typed now, as TypeScript compiles it where it is called, so that what
` allocates there is found in the order TypeScript finds it. One another pass of a parallel type
` pass published is taken in from it (`adopt`).
if instances.rows[callee].state != .instance-unstarted || adopt(session, callee)
    =
. heapless = (instances.rows[callee].effects /and/ CompilationEffect.no-heap) != 0
if watching-leaves == 0 && !heapless && settle-header(session, callee)
    instances.queue(callee)
    =
if deferring && promise(callee)
    instances.queue(callee)
    =
demand-body(callee)

────────────────────
+ do note-live-call
    - id SyntaxId
    - name Atom

demand-live-runtime()
. live = instances.live
if live.enter == no-instance || live.leave == no-instance
    decline(id)
    =
if frame.declaration.kind != .live-decl
    . context = live-context(read-site(id))
    if context == .live-value && is-eager-value()
        instances.mark-live(instance)
    else if context == .live-rule && is-rule-unit()
        instances.mark-live(instance)
    else if context == .live-statement
        note-live-statement(read-site(id))
    else if context != .live-region && context != .live-gate
        frame.diagnose
            - id
            - .stated
            - program.store-atom
                - "The live function \"${name.text}\" is called only where a value is read live"
        =
facts.set-plan(instance, id, .plan-live-call)

────────────────────
+ do check-rerun
    - statement SyntaxId

` The function a live action runs a live statement again with, as the reference compiles it: the
` statement typed again as the body of a closure, which answers nothing. A declaration's value is
` typed again and stored in the local it declares, which must hold it as it is; one some read tracks
` is stored through the list of subscribers it reaches. An attribute's value is typed again for the
` property of the element's object it names, kept where the element was made, or for the style
` property it declares, and an argument of an element for the property its parameter names, and so
` is the value of a line of a style rule for the property of the object it is applied to. A line
` of an element's body is absorbed again by the element, kept where it was made (`absorb-again`), or
` replaces what it took (`replace-again`). The value of a stream of a value as it changes is written
` again to its channel (`stream-again`). An error that leaves the statement is given to
` `unhandled-error` (`hand-off-outgoing`).
prepare()
instances.set-returns(instance, types.void-type, types.void-type, .return-declared)
do match? tree.nodes[statement]
    | .node-iterable-expression(row)
        if !stream-again(statement, row.expr)
            decline(statement)
        hand-off-outgoing(statement)
        finish-errors(frame)
        close()
        =
if tree.content-line(statement)
    . kept = line-keeper(statement)
    . made = if kept != no-slot then frame.slot-type(kept) else no-type
    . previous = if kept != no-slot then frame.slot-type(kept + 1) else no-type
    . absorbs = previous == types.void-type
    if made == no-type || previous == no-type || (absorbs && !absorb-again(statement, made)) || (!absorbs && !replace-again(statement, made, previous))
        decline(statement)
    hand-off-outgoing(statement)
    finish-errors(frame)
    close()
    =
. element = tree.argument-element(statement)
if element != 0
    . resolution = bindings.resolution-of(frame.binding, element)
    . made = if resolution.kind == .resolve-slot then frame.slot-type(resolution.slot) else no-type
    if made == no-type
        decline(statement)
    else
        do argument-again(statement, made)
    hand-off-outgoing(statement)
    finish-errors(frame)
    close()
    =
. bound = tree.bound-attribute(statement)
if bound != 0
    if !bind-again(statement, bound)
        decline(statement)
    hand-off-outgoing(statement)
    finish-errors(frame)
    close()
    =
if tree.attribute-element(statement) != 0
    . resolution = bindings.resolution-of(frame.binding, statement)
    . made = if resolution.kind == .resolve-slot then frame.slot-type(resolution.slot) else no-type
    . styled = facts.style-declaration-of(instances.rows[instance].enclosing, statement)
    do match? tree.nodes[statement]
        | .node-assign(row)
            . name = style-name(tree, row.lhs)
            if styled
                if made == no-type || !style-again(statement, row.rhs, styled)
                    decline(statement)
            else if made == no-type
                decline(statement)
            else if name && attribute-accessor(made, name)
                do setter-attribute(statement, row.op, row.lhs, row.rhs, made)
            else if attribute-type(statement, row.op, row.lhs, row.rhs, made) == invalid-type
                decline(statement)
    hand-off-outgoing(statement)
    finish-errors(frame)
    close()
    =
if facts.rule-update-of(instances.rows[instance].enclosing, statement)
    . resolution = bindings.resolution-of(frame.binding, statement)
    . made = if resolution.kind == .resolve-slot then frame.slot-type(resolution.slot) else no-type
    do match? tree.nodes[statement]
        | .node-assign(row)
            if unmade || attribute-type(statement, row.op, row.lhs, row.rhs, made) == invalid-type
                decline(statement)
            .. unmade = made == no-type
    hand-off-outgoing(statement)
    finish-errors(frame)
    close()
    =
do match tree.nodes[statement]
    | .node-declare(declaration)
        . slot = declaring-slot(declaration.left)
        . value = if slot then infer-declared(declaration.left, declaration.right) else invalid-type
        . tracked = slot && (bindings.slots[slot].flags /and/ SlotFlag.slot-tracked) != 0
        if !slot || value == invalid-type || value != frame.slot-type(slot)
            decline(statement)
        else if tracked && !frame.is-captured(subscribers-slot(slot))
            decline(statement)
        else if tracked
            demand-live-runtime()
    ??
        check-statement(statement)
hand-off-outgoing(statement)
finish-errors(frame)
close()

────────────────────
_ do bind-again Bool
    - anchor SyntaxId
    - statement SyntaxId

. resolution = bindings.resolution-of(frame.binding, statement)
. made = if resolution.kind == .resolve-slot then frame.slot-type(resolution.slot) else no-type
. name = tree.identifier-name(anchor)
=? false if made == no-type || !name
. found = property-named(made, name)
=? false if !found || types.properties[found].storage-kind != .storage-eager
. property = types.properties[found]
. declared = if property.type != no-type then property.type else demand-member(property, made, name)
=? false if declared == no-type || declared == invalid-type
. ref = class-ref(types, types.tracked-root(property.owner, name))
facts.note-tracked(ref.module, ref.decl, name)
instances.mark-may-panic(instance)
demand-live-runtime()
do match? tree.nodes[statement]
    | .node-assign(row)
        standing = anchor
        standing-type = if takes-held(declared, named-place-type(row.rhs)) then types.optional-inner(declared) else declared
        . stored = infer-assign(anchor, .eq-op, row.rhs, anchor, Want())
        standing = 0
        standing-type = no-type
        =? false if stored == invalid-type || stored == no-type
        . held = place-type(row.rhs)
        if held != declared && held != no-type && held != invalid-type && writes-back(declared)
            =? false if conversions.convert(statement, row.rhs, held, declared, .reason-assignment) == invalid-type
        = true
= false

────────────────────
_ do takes-held Bool
    - property TypeId
    - place TypeId

=? false if !types.is-optional(property) || place == no-type || place == invalid-type || types.is-optional(place)
=? false if relations.implicit(conversions.compare-held(property, place))
= relations.implicit(conversions.compare-held(types.optional-inner(property), place))

────────────────────
_ do named-place-type TypeId
    - place SyntaxId

do match? tree.nodes[place]
    | .node-get-expression(row)
        = member-type(named-place-type(row.object), row.name)
= place-type(place)

────────────────────
_ do place-type TypeId
    - place SyntaxId

do match? tree.nodes[place]
    | .node-identifier(row)
        . resolution = bindings.resolution-of(frame.binding, place)
        if resolution.kind == .resolve-slot
            = frame.slot-type(resolution.slot)
        if resolution.kind == .resolve-member
            = member-type(frame.self-type, row.name)
    | .node-get-expression(row)
        = member-type(facts.node-type(instance, row.object), row.name)
= no-type

────────────────────
_ writes-back Bool
    - type TypeId

intrinsic-is-numeric(intrinsic) || intrinsic == .bool

.. intrinsic = types.intrinsic-of(type)

────────────────────
+ do demand-rules
    - receiver TypeId
    - site SyntaxId
    - body SyntaxId = 0

` Types the rules of a class being made and of the classes above it, each for the class that
` writes it as the receiver holds it: the constructor runs them once its body has run, or
` the function that fills the object with the markup of the class that writes one runs it once
` that markup has (`waits-for-markup`), so what they run may panic, and the errors a section
` lets out as it subscribes leave the constructor at `site`. A `when` or `whenever` rule the
` constructor runs gives the object a live action (`own-markup-actions`), and one on the markup
` the object is in registers the object as its markup host (`host-self`). The errors such a
` rule lets out the first time it runs leave the constructor at `site`, and those it lets out
` when its action runs it again are handed off (`hands-off`), as the reference does; one that
` runs on the markup, or once the markup of its class has, that lets out errors has no shape
` here. A dependency the
` class that writes it subscribes otherwise than the object's class would, as one is a markup
` host and the other is not, has no shape here, nor have rules where the
` constructor's body returns before its end, unless each is a section the event runtime runs
` from the table of the class, which no object subscribes. Which sections those are is
` planned first, since it decides how they are typed. One function fills the objects of
` every class below the one that writes the markup, while the reference makes one for each
` class it constructs: a section run there that some such class runs from its table and
` another subscribes has no shape here, and nor has one that lets out errors.
if receiver == no-type || receiver == invalid-type || types.intrinsic-of(receiver) != .class
    =
plan-event-handlers(receiver, site)
. level TypeId? = receiver
. found = false
. ran = false
while level
    for ref in sheet-parts(class-ref(types, level))
        . owner = program.modules[ref.module]
        for member in owner.member-pool[part-members(ref)]
            . written SyntaxId = 0
            do match? owner.decls[member]
                | .decl-rule(rule)
                    written = rule.syntax
            if written == 0
                continue
            found = true
            . section = section-loop(ref.module, written)
            . tabled = facts.lowers(receiver, ref.module, section)
            . waits = waits-for-markup(level, ref.module, written)
            if waits && tabled && facts.holds-section(subscriptions, level, ref.module, section)
                decline(site)
                =
            .. subscriptions = facts.subscribed-sections
            if dependency-line && is-markup-host(receiver) != is-markup-host(level)
                decline(site)
                =
            .. dependency-line = owner.tree.nodes[written] is .node-dependency-declaration
            if !waits && owner.tree.is-live-rule(written)
                live-owned = true
            if owner.tree.is-markup-trigger(written) && !host-self(receiver, site)
                decline(site)
                =
            if !ran && !tabled
                ran = true
                if body != 0 && tree.leaves-early(body)
                    decline(body)
                    =
            . unit = instances.intern-initializer(ref.module, member, level)
            demand-body(unit)
            if waits && !facts.waits-for-markup(unit)
                facts.markup-rules += unit
            if waits && section != 0 && !tabled
                demand-errors(unit)
                if instances.signatures[unit].errors.count != 0
                    decline(site)
                    =
            if section != 0
                note-unit-errors(unit, site)
            else if owner.tree.is-live-rule(written)
                demand-errors(unit)
                if instances.signatures[unit].errors.count != 0
                    if waits || owner.tree.is-markup-trigger(written) || !hands-off(unit)
                        decline(site)
                        =
                    note-unit-errors(unit, site)
    level = types.base-of(level)
if found
    instances.mark-may-panic(instance)

────────────────────
+ do waits-in-rule Bool

` Whether the instance types a rule of a class that runs once the markup of the class has.
. unit = instances.rows[instance]
if unit.initializer == 0 || frame.self-type == no-type
    = false
do match? program.modules[unit.module].decls[unit.initializer]
    | .decl-rule(row)
        = waits-for-markup(frame.self-type, unit.module, row.syntax)
= false

────────────────────
_ do plan-event-handlers
    - receiver TypeId
    - site SyntaxId

` The sections of a class being made, and of the classes above it, base first, that the
` reference runs from a table of the class rather than subscribing them for each object, as it
` plans them once for the class. Each section on an event of the object itself, its name alone
` or read from `this` in a loop of one header, counts among those of the event in order. One
` is run from the table where no section before it on the event was subscribed, the event is
` not published by key, no constructor of the class or of one above it subscribes to the event,
` its loop has no clause but one `when arrival` or `when bubbling`, and its body neither leaves
` it, writes a function, nor names an argument of a constructor of the class that writes it. The
` event runtime's `event-register-lowered` puts it in the table, or its
` `event-register-lowered-arrival` where it hears only what arrives at its object. A section run from the table for every class
` planned when it is typed is typed so alone; a class planned after that which subscribes it
` has no shape here. A class whose chain writes no section has nothing to plan. A class planned
` already is found by its type. An edit typed again in place keeps the plans, as long as it does
` not change what the constructors it edits subscribe to (`retype-edit`).
for planned in facts.lowered-types
    if planned == receiver
        =
. chain [TypeId]
. level TypeId? = receiver
while level
    chain += level
    level = types.base-of(level)
if !writes-sections(chain)
    =
facts.lowered-types += receiver
. heard = constructor-events(receiver, chain)
. owners [TypeId]
. names [Atom]
. counts [U32]
. closed [Bool]
for offset in 0 .. < chain.length
    . holder = chain[chain.length - 1 - offset]
    for ref in sheet-parts(class-ref(types, holder))
        . owner = program.modules[ref.module]
        for member in owner.member-pool[part-members(ref)]
            . syntax SyntaxId = 0
            do match? owner.decls[member]
                | .decl-rule(rule)
                    syntax = rule.syntax
            . found = section-event(receiver, ref.module, syntax) if syntax != 0
            if !found
                continue
            . event = found
            . index = owners.length
            for position in 0 .. < owners.length
                if owners[position] == event.owner && names[position] == event.name
                    index = position
            if index == owners.length
                owners += event.owner
                names += event.name
                counts += 0
                closed += false
            . order = counts[index]
            counts[index] = order + 1
            . subscribed = false
            for other in heard
                if other.owner == event.owner && other.name == event.name
                    subscribed = true
            . iterator = section-loop(ref.module, syntax)
            . arrives = section-delivery(ref.module, syntax) == 1
            if open-event && lowerable-section && facts.event-register == no-instance
                demand-event-register()
            .. open-event = event.key == no-type && !closed[index] && !subscribed
            .. lowerable-section = lowerable(ref.module, ref.decl, syntax)
            . registers = if arrives then facts.event-register-arrival else facts.event-register
            if closed-event || not-lowered || registers == no-instance
                closed[index] = true
                if facts.holds-section(facts.lowered-sections, holder, ref.module, iterator)
                    decline(site)
                if !facts.holds-section(facts.subscribed-sections, holder, ref.module, iterator)
                    facts.subscribed-sections += SectionRef(holder, ref.module, iterator)
                continue
            .. closed-event = event.key != no-type || closed[index] || subscribed
            .. not-lowered = !lowerable(ref.module, ref.decl, syntax)
            facts.lowered-handlers += LoweredHandler
                - receiver
                - holder
                - ref.module
                - member
                - iterator
                - event.owner
                - event.name
                - order
                - arrives

────────────────────
_ do writes-sections Bool
    - chain [TypeId]

` Whether a class of a chain writes a section.
for holder in chain
    for ref in sheet-parts(class-ref(types, holder))
        . owner = program.modules[ref.module]
        for member in owner.member-pool[part-members(ref)]
            do match? owner.decls[member]
                | .decl-rule(rule)
                    if section-loop(ref.module, rule.syntax) != 0
                        = true
= false

────────────────────
_ do section-delivery U32
    - module ModuleId
    - syntax SyntaxId

` Which publications the loop a section of a class writes hears where its only clause says so:
` 1 for `when arrival`, 2 for `when bubbling`, and else 0.
. tree = program.modules[module].tree
do match? tree.nodes[section-loop(module, syntax)]
    | .node-for-block(block)
        do match? tree.nodes[block.loop]
            | .node-loop-syntax(loop)
                = tree.clause-delivery(loop.clause)
= 0

────────────────────
_ do lowerable Bool
    - module ModuleId
    - writer DeclId
    - syntax SyntaxId

` Whether the loop of a section has no clause but one `when arrival` or `when bubbling`, and its
` body has no `break`, no return, no function written in it, and no name of an argument of a
` constructor of the class that writes it, nor of the stream a loop is given.
. owner = program.modules[module]
. tree = owner.tree
. iterator = section-loop(module, syntax)
. body SyntaxId = 0
do match? tree.nodes[iterator]
    | .node-for-block(block)
        body = block.body
        do match? tree.nodes[block.loop]
            | .node-loop-syntax(loop)
                if loop.clause != 0 && tree.clause-delivery(loop.clause) == 0
                    = false
if body == 0
    = false
. arguments [Atom]
do match? owner.decls[writer]
    | .decl-class(class)
        for member in owner.member-pool[class.members]
            do match? owner.decls[member]
                | .decl-function(fn)
                    if fn.kind == .constructor-decl && !fn.is-generated
                        for shape in owner.arg-pool[fn.args]
                            if shape.name
                                arguments += shape.name
for node in tree.subtree-start(body) .. body
    do match? tree.nodes[node]
        | .node-break
            = false
        | .node-return
            = false
        | .node-return-if-true
            = false
        | .node-function-syntax
            = false
        | .node-identifier(row)
            if row.name.text == "(stream)"
                = false
            for name in arguments
                if name == row.name
                    = false
= true

────────────────────
+ do rule-target TypeId
    - written ModuleId
    - syntax SyntaxId
    - env TypeEnv

` The class a `whenever children T` or `whenever descendants T` rule looks for, written in a
` module and evaluated with the type parameters an environment gives, where it is a markup
` host, or no type.
. owner = program.modules[written]
do match? owner.tree.nodes[syntax]
    | .node-whenever-rule-syntax(rule)
        if rule.kind.text != "children" && rule.kind.text != "descendants"
            = no-type
        . type = types.evaluate-type(written, owner.tree, rule.target-type, env)
        = if is-markup-host(type) then type else no-type
= no-type

────────────────────
+ do prune-cells [ScopeUse]
    - first U32
    - uses [ScopeUse]

` The rules written in rules given, with the state cells made from `first` on that none of them
` is under, innermost or further out, taken away again, and those kept renumbered.
. used [Bool]
for _ in first .. < (facts.scope-cells.length as U32)
    used += false
for use in uses
    . chain [U32]
    facts.link-cells(use.outer-cells, chain)
    if use.cell < U32.max - 1
        chain += use.cell
    for held in chain
        if held >= first
            used[held - first] = true
. moved [U32]
. next = first
for index in first .. < (facts.scope-cells.length as U32)
    if used[index - first]
        moved += next
        . holder = facts.scope-cells[index].instance
        if holder != instance && holder != no-instance
            facts.revised += 1
        facts.scope-cells[next] = facts.scope-cells[index]
        next += 1
    else
        moved += U32.max
while (facts.scope-cells.length as U32) > next
    facts.scope-cells.pop()
. kept [ScopeUse]
for use in uses
    . cell = if relocated then moved[use.cell - first] else use.cell
        .. relocated = use.cell >= first && use.cell < U32.max - 1
    . chain [U32]
    facts.link-cells(use.outer-cells, chain)
    . links = U32.max
    for held in chain
        links = facts.scope-link(if held >= first then moved[held - first] else held, links)
    kept += ScopeUse(use.scope, cell, use.values, links)
= kept

────────────────────
+ do scope-cell U32
    - site SyntaxId
    - owner TypeId
    - module ModuleId
    - branch SyntaxId

` The state cell of a `when` at a site of this instance, made once, as the reference keeps one
` for each `when` an element or a class's content sees (`StyleScopeStateCells`), with where it is
` made (`cell-key`). While the way to a slot outlet is followed (`discovering`), one of no
` instance, which the function that builds what the outlet mounts reads from those it holds.
. holder = if keying.discovering then no-instance else instance
. key = cell-key(site, module, branch)
for index in 0 .. < facts.scope-cells.length
    . held = facts.scope-cells[index]
    if same-site && held.when == branch && held.key == key
        = index as U32
    .. same-site = held.instance == holder && held.site == site && held.module == module
facts.scope-cells += ScopeCell(holder, site, module, branch, owner, false, U32.max, key)
= (facts.scope-cells.length - 1) as U32

────────────────────
_ do cell-key U32
    - site SyntaxId
    - written ModuleId
    - branch SyntaxId

` Where the state cell of a `when`, written in `written`, made at a site of this instance is made,
` among `Instances.state-keys`, as the reference's `styleScopeStateKey` keys it: the markup element,
` or where `keying` names one, the root `<This`, class, or element of markup it names, in its
` module.
if keying.site != 0
    = instances.state-key(keying.module, keying.site, written, branch)
= instances.state-key(module, site, written, branch)

────────────────────
+ do take-cell U32
    - cell U32

` A state cell the function building markup sees as the markup it is written in sees it, as
` `take-scope` says.
if facts.scope-cells[cell].instance == no-instance
    = read-cell(cell)
= kept-cell(cell)

────────────────────
_ do kept-cell U32
    - source U32

` The state cell this function keeps of one of the function it is written in, made once, in the
` order kept. It names that one's cell, so this function is typed only with that one
` (`Instance.with-enclosing`).
instances.rows[instance].with-enclosing = true
. count U32
for index in 0 .. < facts.scope-cells.length
    . held = facts.scope-cells[index]
    if held.instance == instance && held.kept != U32.max
        if held.source == source
            = index as U32
        count += 1
. row = facts.scope-cells[source]
facts.scope-cells += ScopeCell
    - instance
    - U32.max
    - row.module
    - row.when
    - row.owner
    - true
    - U32.max
    - row.key
    - count
    - source
= (facts.scope-cells.length - 1) as U32

────────────────────
_ do read-cell U32
    - found U32

` The state cell this function reads from those the slot outlet that mounts what it builds holds,
` for one found on the way there, made once for each place a cell is made, as the reference's
` `markupStyleRuleScopesWithOutletStates` reads one. False where the runtime has no such read.
. row = facts.scope-cells[found]
for index in 0 .. < facts.scope-cells.length
    . held = facts.scope-cells[index]
    if held.instance == instance && held.read && held.key == row.key
        = index as U32
do demand-outlet-states()
facts.scope-cells += ScopeCell
    - instance
    - U32.max
    - row.module
    - row.when
    - row.owner
    - true
    - U32.max
    - row.key
    - U32.max
    - U32.max
    - true
= (facts.scope-cells.length - 1) as U32

────────────────────
+ do hold-cells Bool
    - id SyntaxId
    - uses [ScopeUse]

` Keeps the state cells a slot outlet holds while the function that builds what it mounts runs, or
` a line that forwards a slot while the builder it forwards does (`OutletCell`), as the reference's
` `markupOutletStyleStateCells` takes them: of the rules written in rules `uses`, the cells of the
` `when`s around each, the outermost first, the first for each place cells are made, but those
` given with the context, which no place made. False where the runtime has none.
. keys [U32]
. cells [U32]
for use in uses
    if use.cell >= U32.max - 1
        continue
    . chain [U32]
    facts.link-cells(use.outer-cells, chain)
    chain += use.cell
    for held in chain
        . key = facts.scope-cells[held].key
        if key != U32.max && keys.find(key) == null
            keys += key
            cells += held
if cells.length == 0
    = true
if !demand-outlet-states()
    decline(id)
    = false
for held in facts.outlet-cells
    if held.instance == instance && held.outlet == id
        = true
for cell in cells
    facts.outlet-cells += OutletCell(instance, id, cell)
= true

────────────────────
+ do given-cell U32
    - scope RuleScope
    - argument U32
    - depth U32

` The state cell this instance is given, its `argument`th, for a `when` around a rule written in
` a rule its context gives: the frame of the rule that is the `depth`th `when`'s from the
` innermost. It is made at no place a slot outlet holds it by, as the reference's
` `markupStyleContextWithRuntimeValues` drops the `stateKey` of the frames a function is given.
. frame = scope.frames
. passed U32
while frame != U32.max
    if instances.frames[frame].gate != 0
        if passed == depth
            break
        passed += 1
    frame = instances.frames[frame].outer
. module = if frame != U32.max then instances.frames[frame].module else 0u32
. branch = if frame != U32.max then instances.frames[frame].gate else 0u32
facts.scope-cells += ScopeCell(instance, U32.max, module, branch, no-type, true, argument)
= (facts.scope-cells.length - 1) as U32

────────────────────
+ do check-cells Bool
    - site SyntaxId
    - at SyntaxId
    - made TypeId
    - known Bool

` Checks the state each state cell made at a site names, once, as the reference binds them once
` the object is made (`compileStyleScopeStateBindings`): a property of the class of the object,
` `made`, of type `Bool`, as the reference reports, which is read tracked. Where the class was
` not `known` exactly, which is where the cell is made for a class's content that classes below
` may run, one the class has not is declined. False where one is reported or declined.
for index in 0 .. < facts.scope-cells.length
    . held = facts.scope-cells[index]
    if held.instance != instance || held.site != site || held.checked
        continue
    facts.scope-cells[index].checked = true
    if !check-cell(held, at, made, known)
        = false
= true

────────────────────
_ do check-cell Bool
    - held ScopeCell
    - at SyntaxId
    - made TypeId
    - known Bool

` Checks the state a state cell names, as `check-cells` says, and types what keeps the cell: the
` constructor of `StyleScopeState`, whose `is-on` is read tracked, and the live action.
. written = program.modules[held.module].tree
. state = program.store-atom("")
do match? written.nodes[held.when]
    | .node-style-when(row)
        state = row.state
. place = property-named(made, state)
. shown = type-short-name(types, made)
if !place
    if !known
        decline(at)
        = false
    facts.record-diagnostic
        - instance
        - held.module
        - held.when
        - .stated
        - program.store-atom("Style state \"${state.text}\" is not a property of $shown")
        - no-type
        - no-type
    = false
. property = types.properties[place]
if property.storage-kind == .storage-getter
    decline(at)
    = false
. declared = property.type
if declared == no-type
    declared = demand-member(property, made, state)
if declared == invalid-type
    = false
if declared != types.bool-type
    facts.record-diagnostic(instance, held.module, held.when, .stated, program.store-atom("Style state \"${state.text}\" must be a boolean property, but $shown.${state.text} is ${type-display(types, declared)}"), declared, no-type)
    = false
instances.mark-may-panic(instance)
. key = panics.property-of(made, state)
if key
    panics.track(key)
. ref = class-ref(types, property.owner)
facts.note-tracked(ref.module, ref.decl, state)
demand-live-runtime()
. cell = types.well-known-type("core/style", "StyleScopeState")
if cell == invalid-type || instances.live.action == no-instance || no-track
    decline(at)
    = false
.. no-track = instances.live.track == no-instance
. runtime = facts.style-runtime
if runtime.scope-state == no-instance
    types.complete(cell)
    runtime.scope-state = calls.demand-constructor(cell, scratch.types.mark)
    facts.style-runtime = runtime
if runtime.scope-state == no-instance
    decline(at)
    = false
. is-on = program.store-atom("is-on")
. cell-key = panics.property-of(cell, is-on)
if cell-key
    panics.track(cell-key)
. cell-ref = class-ref(types, cell)
facts.note-tracked(cell-ref.module, cell-ref.decl, is-on)
= true

────────────────────
_ do promise Bool
    - callee InstanceId

` Gives a rule that states its type what its function returns, the optional of that type,
` from its declaration alone, so that its body may wait in the queue. False for any other
` instance, whose body says what it returns.
. row = instances.rows[callee]
if row.self-type != no-type || row.enclosing != no-instance || row.holds-closure || no-rule
    = false
.. no-rule = rule-match(program, row.module, row.decl) == 0
. reported = facts.diagnostics.length
. checker = checker-for(session, callee)
. declared = no-type
if checker.described
    checker.prepare()
    declared = checker.declared-return
    checker.close()
checker.retire()
facts.diagnostics.truncate(reported)
if declared == no-type || declared == invalid-type
    = false
. stated = types.optional-around(declared)
instances.set-returns(callee, stated, stated, .return-declared)
= true

────────────────────
+ do check-class-rule
    - receiver TypeId
    - syntax SyntaxId
    - writer DeclId

` Types a rule of a class for the class that writes it, as the value of a property is typed:
` with `this` bound and the type parameters of that class as the receiver gives them. What a
` `when` rule tests is tested for truth, as a condition is, and the rule's value is what a
` `whenever` rule compares from one run to the next. A rule answers nothing. The reference
` reports one that reads nothing tracked where it runs it in a live action of its own: a
` `when` rule as it tests and runs its body, a `whenever` rule as it takes its value. A section
` that subscribes to a stream is typed as its loop, which the object owns; one on a stream of
` an element a branch of the markup makes is subscribed again as the branch makes the element
` again (`rebind-section`). How a section is typed is noted as the instance's (`TypedSection`).
frame.self-type = receiver
bind-this(receiver)
frame.close-env()
open-class-env(holding-type(receiver, DeclRef(module, writer)))
do match? tree.nodes[syntax]
    | .node-when-rule-syntax(rule)
        note-truthiness(rule.expr, rule.expr, infer(rule.expr))
        check-statement(rule.body)
        untracked-rule(rule.expr, "when rules must read at least one tracked property")
    | .node-whenever-rule-syntax(rule)
        if rule.kind.text != "value"
            check-markup-trigger(receiver, syntax, rule)
        else
            . value = infer(rule.expr)
            if untracked-rule(rule.expr, "whenever value triggers must read at least one tracked property (like #bar)")
                demand-change-test(rule.expr, value)
            check-statement(rule.body)
    | .node-dependency-declaration(dependency)
        check-dependency(receiver, syntax, dependency.left, dependency.right)
    | .node-subscriber-syntax(section)
        do match? tree.nodes[section.iterator]
            | .node-for-block(row)
                . root = branch-root(receiver, row.loop)
                if root == 0 || rebind-section(receiver, section.iterator, row.loop, root)
                    . lowered = facts.lowers-only(receiver, module, section.iterator)
                    if lowered
                        lowering = section.iterator
                        if !facts.holds-section(sections, receiver, module, section.iterator)
                            facts.lowered-sections += SectionRef(receiver, module, section.iterator)
                        .. sections = facts.lowered-sections
                    facts.typed-sections += TypedSection
                        - instance
                        - receiver
                        - module
                        - section.iterator
                        - lowered
                    rebound-root = root
                    check-for(section.iterator, row.loop, row.body, 0)
                    rebound-root = 0
                    lowering = 0
instances.set-returns(instance, types.void-type, types.void-type, .return-declared)
finish-errors(frame)
close()

────────────────────
_ do rebind-section Bool
    - receiver TypeId
    - iterator SyntaxId
    - loop SyntaxId
    - root SyntaxId

` A section on a stream of an element a branch of the markup makes, which the reference
` subscribes in a live action of its own that reads the element tracked, as its
` `loopAsRebindingSubscription` does: as the branch makes the element again, the action reads
` the stream again and the tracker of a new subscription to it takes the old one's place. The
` element's property is tracked so. A `whenever` clause there is the reference's error.
. clause = tree.whenever-clause(loop)
if clause != 0
    . message = "A whenever clause cannot follow a named element that a branch rebuilds"
    frame.diagnose(clause, .stated, program.store-atom(message))
    = false
. name = tree.identifier-name(root)!
. place = property-named(receiver, name)
if !place
    decline(root)
    = false
demand-live-runtime()
. live = instances.live
. runs = live.action != no-instance && live.previous != no-instance && live.next != no-instance
. adds = live.trackers != no-instance && live.add-tracker != no-instance
if !runs || !adds || live.track == no-instance || live.subscribers == no-instance
    decline(root)
    = false
instances.mark-may-panic(instance)
. key = panics.property-of(receiver, name)
if key
    panics.track(key)
. ref = class-ref(types, types.tracked-root(types.properties[place].owner, name))
facts.note-tracked(ref.module, ref.decl, name)
if !facts.holds-section(facts.rebinding-sections, receiver, module, iterator)
    facts.rebinding-sections += SectionRef(receiver, module, iterator)
= true

────────────────────
_ do branch-root SyntaxId
    - receiver TypeId
    - loop SyntaxId

` The name, read untracked, that the stream a loop of a class's section subscribes to is read
` from, where the markup of the class, or of one above it, gives that name an element written
` in an `if` or a `match` of that markup, outside its functions and loops, or none.
. root SyntaxId = 0
do match? tree.nodes[loop]
    | .node-loop-syntax(row)
        root = row.container
. reached = false
while !reached
    do match tree.nodes[root]
        | .node-get-expression(get)
            root = get.object
        ??
            reached = true
. name Atom? = null
do match? tree.nodes[root]
    | .node-identifier(read)
        if !read.is-tracked
            name = read.name
if !name
    = 0
. level TypeId? = receiver
while level
    . ref = class-ref(types, level)
    do match? program.modules[ref.module].decls[ref.decl]
        | .decl-class(class)
            if class.content != 0 && owner-tree.branches-element(class.content, name)
                = root
            .. owner-tree = program.modules[ref.module].tree
    level = types.base-of(level)
= 0

────────────────────
_ do required-argument Atom?
    - receiver TypeId
    - method Atom

` The first argument a class's method of a name requires, where each method of that name the
` class declares requires one, which a dependency, calling it with nothing, cannot give; none
` where one requires none, or the class declares none.
. ref = class-ref(types, receiver)
. owner = program.modules[ref.module]
. required Atom? = null
do match? owner.decls[ref.decl]
    | .decl-class(row)
        for member in owner.member-pool[row.members]
            do match? owner.decls[member]
                | .decl-function(fn)
                    if fn.name && fn.name == method
                        . first = first-required(owner, fn)
                        if !first
                            = null
                        required = first
= required

────────────────────
_ do first-required Atom?
    - owner Module
    - fn FunctionDecl

` The name of the first argument a function requires: one with no default that is not variadic.
for offset in 0 .. < fn.args.count
    . shape = owner.arg-pool[fn.args.start + offset]
    if !shape.has-default && !shape.is-variadic
        = shape.name ?? program.store-atom("_")
= null

────────────────────
_ do check-dependency
    - receiver TypeId
    - syntax SyntaxId
    - left SyntaxId
    - right RowRange'SyntaxId

` A dependency `. m < p, q` of a class: each property it names is tracked, and the method is
` read as a value of the object being made, given as a `Doer` to `property-dependency-subscribe`
` once for each property, or for an object of a markup host to the markup runtime's
` `markup-property-dependency-subscribe`, given the object as its host too. The conversions are
` recorded at the dependency, where the reference places the call the `Doer` makes. The
` reference reports a property or a method the class does not have. A getter is never stored, so
` a dependency on it would never run, and is reported.
for name-syntax in tree.children[right]
    . name = tree.identifier-atom(name-syntax)
    . place = property-named(receiver, name) if name
    if !place
        . shown = if name then name.text else ""
        frame.diagnose(syntax, .stated, program.store-atom("Property \"$shown\" does not exist"))
        =
    if types.properties[place].storage-kind == .storage-getter
        . text = "\"${name!.text}\" is a getter, which is never stored, so a dependency on it never runs; depend on the properties it reads"
        frame.diagnose(name-syntax, .stated, program.store-atom(text))
        =
    . ref = class-ref(types, types.tracked-root(types.properties[place].owner, name!))
    facts.note-tracked(ref.module, ref.decl, name!)
. method = tree.identifier-atom(left)
. bound = if method then calls.method-binding(receiver, method, left) else no-type
if bound == invalid-type
    =
if bound == no-type
    . shown = if method then method.text else ""
    frame.diagnose(syntax, .stated, program.store-atom("Function \"$shown\" does not exist"))
    =
. required = required-argument(receiver, method!)
if required
    . text = "A dependency calls \"${method!.text}\" with nothing, but it takes \"${required.text}\"; give \"${required.text}\" a default, or name a method that takes nothing"
    frame.diagnose(left, .stated, program.store-atom(text))
    =
. doer = types.well-known-type("core/function", "Doer")
if doer == invalid-type
    decline(syntax)
    =
facts.set-node-type(instance, left, bound)
conversions.convert(syntax, left, bound, doer, .reason-argument)
demand-live-runtime()
. hosted = is-markup-host(receiver)
. host = if hosted then derived-interface(receiver, types.markup-host-decl) else no-type
. mark = scratch.types.mark
scratch.types.push(receiver)
if hosted
    scratch.types.push(host)
scratch.types.push(types.string-type)
scratch.types.push(doer)
. module = if hosted then types.markup-host-decl.module else live-module
    .. live-module = class-ref(types, types.live-action-type).module
. subscribe = calls.demand-runtime-call
    - module
    - no-type
    - program.store-atom
        - if hosted then "markup-property-dependency-subscribe" else "property-dependency-subscribe"
    - mark
scratch.types.rewind(mark)
if subscribe == no-instance
    decline(syntax)
    =
if hosted
    conversions.convert(syntax, syntax, receiver, host, .reason-markup-host)
facts.note-change-test(instance, subscribe, hosted)

────────────────────
_ do untracked-rule Bool
    - expr SyntaxId
    - message String

` Reports a rule that has read nothing tracked so far, unless what it read has no shape here;
` whether it has read something.
if instances.rows[instance].is-live
    = true
if !facts.declined-since(0, instance)
    frame.diagnose(expr, .stated, program.store-atom(message))
= false

────────────────────
_ do demand-change-test
    - expr SyntaxId
    - value TypeId

` The function that tells whether a `whenever` rule's value has changed, given the value it
` had and the one it has: `value-changed` of the tracker's runtime, for the value's type.
if value == no-type || value == invalid-type
    =
. mark = scratch.types.mark
scratch.types.push(value)
scratch.types.push(value)
. module = class-ref(types, types.live-action-type).module
. tester = calls.demand-runtime-call(module, no-type, program.store-atom("value-changed"), mark)
scratch.types.rewind(mark)
if tester == no-instance
    decline(expr)
    =
facts.note-change-test(instance, tester)

────────────────────
+ do demand-live-action-cleanup

. action = types.live-action-type
if action == invalid-type
    =
. mark = scratch.types.mark
scratch.types.push(action)
. actions = types.class-named-with-args(module, types.list-atom!, mark)
calls.demand-method(actions, program.store-atom("!"))
calls.demand-method(actions, program.store-atom("pop"))
calls.demand-method(action, program.store-atom("close"))

────────────────────
_ do replace-again Bool
    - statement SyntaxId
    - made TypeId
    - previous TypeId

` Types a line of a markup element's body that a live action gives the element again in place
` of what it took before, kept where the element was made, as the reference's replacer gives it:
` a markup host makes the value its node by its `markup-content`, which the markup runtime's
` `markup-replace` puts in place of the one before; another element's `replace` is given the
` one before and the value, and what it answers, or the value where it answers nothing, is kept
` in place of the one before. That is then closed by its `close`, or where it has none, each
` live action it owns is. What is kept is of the type of what was kept before.
content-blocks += 0
content-parents += made
content-names += false
. produced = infer(statement)
content-blocks.pop()
content-parents.pop()
content-names.pop()
if produced == invalid-type || produced == no-type
    = false
. taken = produced
. call = no-fact
. replace = no-instance
. kept = produced
if is-markup-host(made)
    . content = calls.content-call(made, program.store-atom("markup-content"), statement, produced)
    taken = content.taken
    call = content.fact
    kept = content.answer
    if taken == no-type || call == no-fact || kept != previous
        = false
    . mark = scratch.types.mark
    scratch.types.push(made)
    scratch.types.push(previous)
    scratch.types.push(kept)
    replace = calls.demand-runtime-call
        - types.markup-host-decl.module
        - no-type
        - program.store-atom("markup-replace")
        - mark
    scratch.types.rewind(mark)
    if replace == no-instance
        = false
    conversions.convert(statement, statement, produced, taken, .reason-argument)
else
    . given [TypeId]
    given += previous
    given += produced
    . replacing = calls.protocol-call(made, program.store-atom("replace"), statement, given)
    call = replacing.fact
    if call == no-fact || replacing.answer == invalid-type
        = false
    if replacing.answer != no-type
        kept = replacing.answer
    if kept != previous
        = false
. nothing [TypeId]
. closed = calls.protocol-call(previous, program.store-atom("close"), statement, nothing).fact
if closed == no-fact
    demand-live-runtime()
    if instances.live.has-actions == no-instance
        = false
facts.note-content-link
    - ContentLink(instance, statement, made, taken, call, no-type, replace, closed)
= true

────────────────────
_ do absorb-again Bool
    - statement SyntaxId
    - made TypeId

` Types a line of a markup element's body that a live action gives the element again: its value,
` where a name of a member of the element is read from the element's object, kept where the
` element was made, is absorbed again by the element's `markup-absorb`, as where it is written.
content-blocks += 0
content-parents += made
content-names += false
. produced = infer(statement)
content-blocks.pop()
content-parents.pop()
content-names.pop()
if produced == invalid-type || produced == no-type
    = false
. absorbing = calls.content-call(made, program.store-atom("markup-absorb"), statement, produced)
. absorbed = absorbing.taken
if absorbed == no-type
    = false
conversions.convert(statement, statement, produced, absorbed, .reason-argument)
facts.note-content-link(ContentLink(instance, statement, made, absorbed, absorbing.fact))
= true

────────────────────
_ do argument-again TypeId
    - arg SyntaxId
    - made TypeId

` The type an argument of a markup element, given by position, is given again by its own
` function: that of the property its parameter names, to which the value is converted as one
` assigned is. A parameter that names no property stored in the object, as the instance that
` makes the element chose its constructor, is declined.
. element = tree.argument-element(arg)
. name = argument-name(arg, element, instances.rows[instance].enclosing)
. place = property-named(made, name) if name
if !place
    decline(arg)
    = invalid-type
. property = types.properties[place]
if property.storage-kind != .storage-eager
    decline(arg)
    = invalid-type
. declared = property.type
if declared == no-type
    declared = demand-member(property, made, name!)
if declared == no-type || declared == invalid-type
    decline(arg)
    = invalid-type
. written = infer(arg)
if written == invalid-type || written == no-type
    = invalid-type
if conversions.convert(arg, arg, written, declared, .reason-assignment) == invalid-type
    = invalid-type
= declared

────────────────────
+ do in-live-statement Bool
    - node SyntaxId
    - body SyntaxId

` Whether a node is written in an assignment, a declaration or an argument of a markup
` element within a body that a function of its own runs again.
for outer in node .. < body
    if tree.subtree-start(outer) <= node && is-live-statement(outer)
        = true
= false

────────────────────
+ do untracked-read SyntaxId
    - id SyntaxId
    - scope Atom

` The first read, in the order written, of a member of what a name names that is not tracked,
` outside a function or a `do` block, or none.
do match? tree.nodes[id]
    | .node-function-syntax
        = 0
    | .node-do-block
        = 0
    | .node-get-expression(row)
        if !row.is-tracked && tree.nodes[row.object] is .node-identifier && reads-scope
            = id
        .. reads-scope = tree.identifier-name(row.object) == scope
for child in tree.children-of(id)
    . found = untracked-read(child, scope)
    if found != 0
        = found
= 0

────────────────────
_ do arm-line SyntaxId
    - region SyntaxId
    - id SyntaxId

` The line of the body of an arm of a markup branch or match region that gives content a node is
` written in, where a function of its own gives it again, or none.
for arm in tree.region-arms(region)
    do match? tree.nodes[tree.region-arm-body(arm)]
        | .node-block(block)
            for line in tree.children[block.body]
                if tree.subtree-start(line) <= id && id <= line
                    = if tree.content-line(line) && is-live-statement(line) then line else 0u32
= 0

────────────────────
_ matched-line SyntaxId
    - arm SyntaxId
    - id SyntaxId

` The line of an arm of a markup match region that gives content a node is written in, as
` `arm-line` says, or none. The arm is not written within its match, which follows it.
if region != 0 && is-region(region) then arm-line(region, id) else 0u32

.. region = tree.arm-match(arm)

────────────────────
+ do check-subscription
    - id SyntaxId
    - loop SyntaxId
    - container SyntaxId
    - clause SyntaxId
    - decl DeclId

` A loop on a stream where it is written, as the reference compiles one with no `whenever`
` clause: the container is made a `Broadcastable`, and the loop's subscriber, a closure of the
` item and the stream, is made a `Subscriber` and given to the broadcaster's `subscribe`, both
` recorded at the `for` block, whose errors leave the function as those of a call written
` there would. One in a method of an object or a section of a class, which the object owns, is
` subscribed as `own-subscription` says, and one with a `whenever` clause as
` `subscribe-whenever` says.
