` `track-local` says, the receiver itself is not, and a global can not be, as the reference
` reports. A name a pattern binds is tracked by the reference through its function's list,
` which nothing stores to by that name unless another local of the function shares it: it is
` read plainly then. Any other name is read plainly where no live action is open, and has no
` shape here yet where one is.
