` be tracked, as the reference reports. Where no live action of the
` reference is open the read is a plain one. In the value of a stored property of a class,
` outside the functions written in it, the value runs in a live action of its own that notes
` the read, and so does a rule of a class, and so does the `whenever` clause of a loop on a
` stream. So does the value of a declaration of a style rule (`unit-styling.styling`). Any
` other read a live action sees has no shape here yet. A field of a struct or a tuple is reported,
` as their values are copied and no object notes what reads them, and so is a read in the value
