` another, which assignments, lazy declarations, markup, streams and subscriptions open, as
` does a function written in a value or a rule. An argument of a markup element run again is a
` live statement, as is a line of its body that gives content. The `keyed by` clause of a markup
` loop region is typed in a function of its own, which the reference compiles where no live
` action is open, and so are the values given rules an element applies, where the element is
` written in lines of markup alone out to a class's markup (`applies-plainly`) or is the root
` `<This`, whose values an instance of their own types, but their conditions, each tested in a
` gate's (`in-condition`). Where those values read something tracked, the rules' declarations
` that read them are declared again as it changes (`values-live`). A closure that is
